{{also|hémisphère}}
{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|hemisphære}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|hemisphaerium}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἡμισφαίριον}}, from {{m|grc|ἡμι-||half}} + {{m|grc|σφαῖρα||sphere}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|en|hemi|sphere}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|healftrendel|lit=half-sphere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛmɪsfɪə/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|hĕ'mĭsfîr|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛmɪsfɪəɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hemisphere.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy|astrology}} Half of the [[celestial sphere]], as divided by either the [[ecliptic]] or the [[celestial equator]] {{defdate|from 14th c.}}.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A realm or domain of activity {{defdate|1503}}.
#* {{RQ:Landon Romance|pages=91–92|volume=III|passage=Love is the Columbus of our moral world, and opens, at some period or other, a new '''hemisphere''' to our view.}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} Half of the [[Earth]], such as the [[Northern Hemisphere]], [[Southern Hemisphere]], [[Western Hemisphere]] or [[Eastern Hemisphere]], [[Land Hemisphere]], [[Water Hemisphere]] etc. {{defdate|1550s}}.
# {{lb|en|geometry}} Any half-[[sphere]], formed by a [[plane]] [[intersect]]ing the center of a sphere. {{defdate|1580s}}.
# {{lb|en|cartography}} A map or projection of a celestial or terrestrial hemisphere {{defdate|1706}}.
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Either of the two [[halves]] of the [[cerebrum]]. {{defdate|1804}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|astronomy: half of the celestial sphere}} {{l|en|celestial hemisphere}}
* {{sense|geography: half of the terrestrial sphere}} {{l|en|terrestrial hemisphere}}
* {{sense|figuratively: a domain of thought or action}} {{l|en|sphere}}
* {{sense|geometry: half of a sphere}} {{l|en|half-sphere}}, {{l|en|half sphere}}
* {{sense|anatomy: either of the two lobes of the cerebellum}} {{l|en|cerebral hemisphere}}
* {{sense|cartography: a map showing a projection of a hemisphere}} {{l|en|planisphere}}

